  "summary": "The Tamil Nadu Dr. Ambedkar Law University was established by Tamil Nadu Act No. 43 of 1997 — the country's first full-fledged affiliating law university. Its School of Excellence in Law, set up in 2002 on its own campus and modelled on the national law schools, offers five-year integrated B.A./B.B.A./B.Com./B.C.A. LL.B. (Hons.) degrees and a three-year LL.B. Admission is on Class XII marks under Tamil Nadu's reservation rules — no entrance test.",
